window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["1b"]={"https://theconversation.com/ethiopias-armed-opposition-unites-against-abiy-ahmed-5-reads-on-the-countrys-political-struggles-292619":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"6ad1822b3393dbe44530bceb0e98e370095e775d17408df646d37faa5b174599","read":"https://theconversation.com/ethiopias-armed-opposition-unites-against-abiy-ahmed-5-reads-on-the-countrys-political-struggles-292619","bytes":183867,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Ethiopia’s armed opposition unites against Abiy Ahmed: 5 reads on the country’s political struggles","by":[{"n":"Julius Maina","r":"Regional Editor East Africa"},{"n":"Kagure Gacheche","r":"Commissioning Editor, East Africa"},{"n":"Alemayehu Fentaw Weldemariam","r":"Adjunct Professor and Ph.D. Fellow, Center for Constitutional Democracy, Indiana University"},{"n":"Dereje Melese Liyew","r":"Lecturer and Reseacher, Political Science, Debre Markos University,"},{"n":"Mohammed Girma","r":"Visiting Lecturer, University of Roehampton"},{"n":"Namhla Thando Matshanda","r":"Associate Professor, Department of Political Sciences, University of Pretoria"},{"n":"Terefe Gebreyesus","r":"Lecturer, Griffith University"}],"pub":"2026-09-22T13:19:33Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Seven Ethiopian armed groups have ",["announced a new alliance","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/ckp84pj8zpngo"]," aimed at overthrowing the government of ",["Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed","https://www.britannica.com/biography/Abiy-Ahmed"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The so-called Ethiopian Peoples’ Forces Alliance for Survival was unveiled in September 2026. It arrives at a time when Abiy is ",["grappling","https://kulu-media.com/ethiopia-accuses-eritrea-of-financing-new-armed-groups-coalition/"]," with armed conflict and deepening political and ethnic divisions. There is fighting in the ",["Amhara region","https://theconversation.com/ethiopias-amhara-people-are-being-portrayed-as-the-enemy-the-dangerous-history-of-ethnic-politics-212626"]," between federal forces and local insurgents. Meanwhile, rising tensions in Tigray have ",["sparked fears of renewed war","https://theconversation.com/conflict-is-rising-in-ethiopias-tigray-region-5-steps-that-could-stop-a-return-to-full-scale-war-290573"],". These are only two flashpoints in a sea of ",["political divisions","https://www.cfr.org/global-conflict-tracker/conflict/conflict-ethiopia"]," that war, elections and national dialogue have so far failed to heal."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Conversation Africa has published extensively on Ethiopia’s attempts to hold the country together. Here are five essential reads."]},{"k":"h","s":["National dialogue struggles to bridge the divide"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ethiopia launched a ",["national dialogue process in 2022","https://justice.gov.et/en/law/the-ethiopian-national-dialogue-commission-establishment-proclamation/"]," after a stop to a ",["two-year war in Tigray","https://www.peaceau.org/en/article/cessation-of-hostilities-agreement-between-the-government-of-the-federal-democratic-republic-of-ethiopia-and-the-tigray-peoples-liberation-front-tplf"],". The process aims to address the grievances that have led to decades of political instability and violence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some political actors have been left out of the process, however. They include armed groups like the Oromo Liberation Army, the Tigray People’s Liberation Front and the Amhara Fano. Yet they are central to ongoing conflicts. They have now become part of the alliance of seven groups against Abiy’s government."]},{"k":"p","s":["In a ",["recent paper","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/02589001.2025.2595933"],", Dereje Melese Liyew examined why the dialogue process is facing a crisis. He ",["explains","https://theconversation.com/ethiopias-national-dialogue-was-meant-to-heal-the-nation-but-divisions-are-deepening-278321"]," its weaknesses and what this means for Ethiopia’s efforts to resolve political conflicts without resorting to violence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Ethiopia’s national dialogue was meant to heal the nation, but divisions are deepening","https://theconversation.com/ethiopias-national-dialogue-was-meant-to-heal-the-nation-but-divisions-are-deepening-278321"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Battle for democracy"]},{"k":"p","s":["Abiy’s arrival in power in 2018 brought ",["hopes of more political freedom","https://theconversation.com/abiy-ahmed-gained-power-in-ethiopia-with-the-help-of-young-people-four-years-later-hes-silencing-them-195601"],". Political prisoners were ",["released","https://www.theguardian.com/world/2018/jul/08/abiy-ahmed-upending-ethiopian-politics"]," and restrictions on the media were eased."]},{"k":"p","s":["But a stable democratic settlement didn’t follow. And the interventions weren’t Ethiopia’s first attempt at democratic governance. A culture of solving political differences with conflict, the absence of strong political institutions and ethnic polarisation have led to disagreements about the Ethiopian state."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terefe Gebreyesus has ",["examined","https://brill.com/view/journals/afoc/37/2/article-p332_6.xml"]," what Ethiopia needs to get democracy right. In ",["his view","https://theconversation.com/ethiopias-two-bids-at-democracy-have-failed-what-it-will-take-to-succeed-263817"],", four things are missing: sustained economic growth, political elites committed to democratic rules, independent political institutions, and international pressure."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Ethiopia’s two bids at democracy have failed: what it will take to succeed","https://theconversation.com/ethiopias-two-bids-at-democracy-have-failed-what-it-will-take-to-succeed-263817"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Ethiopia’s past"]},{"k":"p","s":["One reason building a common political future has been so difficult is that Ethiopians do not ",["share a common interpretation","https://theconversation.com/residual-anger-driven-by-the-politics-of-power-has-boiled-over-into-conflict-in-ethiopia-150327"]," of their past."]},{"k":"p","s":["Political movements have repeatedly drawn on competing ideas about the state, ethnicity, marginalisation and national identity. These histories ",["shape present-day arguments","https://theconversation.com/explainer-why-ethiopias-federal-system-is-deeply-flawed-119313"]," over how Ethiopia should be organised."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ethiopia needs a new rallying point instead of recycling its painful past, ",["argues","https://theconversation.com/ethiopia-needs-a-new-rallying-point-instead-of-recycling-its-painful-past-121531"]," Mohammed Girma. He notes that returning to contested historical narratives can be divisive. Ethiopia instead needs a shared political project that can bring its different communities together."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Ethiopia needs a new rallying point instead of recycling its painful past","https://theconversation.com/ethiopia-needs-a-new-rallying-point-instead-of-recycling-its-painful-past-121531"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Changing leaders won’t fix everything"]},{"k":"p","s":["Debates about Ethiopia’s political future frequently focus on the enormous power of the prime minister. Would ",["term limits","https://www.bbc.com/amharic/articles/cjepddvyvvno"]," help address this?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Under Ethiopia’s system, prime ministers get their authority from parliament. They remain in office for as long as a majority in parliament is willing to support them. There are no fixed term limits."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, limiting an individual leader’s time in office cannot by itself make democratic institutions stronger. The deeper issue is how political power is organised and constrained, says Alemayehu Fentaw Weldemariam, who has ",["studied","https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=en&user=arlPf30AAAAJ&view_op=list_works&sortby=pubdate"]," Ethiopia’s constitutional design and law."]},{"k":"p","s":["He ",["argues that","https://theconversation.com/should-ethiopia-limit-how-long-its-prime-minister-can-serve-why-this-wont-fix-a-deeper-democracy-problem-283405"]," meaningful political competition and mechanisms that make the government accountable matter alongside rules for how long a leader can remain in office."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Should Ethiopia limit how long its prime minister can serve? Why this won’t fix a deeper democracy problem","https://theconversation.com/should-ethiopia-limit-how-long-its-prime-minister-can-serve-why-this-wont-fix-a-deeper-democracy-problem-283405"]]},{"k":"h","s":["What unites Ethiopia?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Amid political fragmentation, Ethiopian leaders have sought symbols capable of creating a shared sense of national purpose. The ",["Grand Ethiopian Renaissance Dam","https://theconversation.com/ethiopias-mega-dam-has-taken-14-years-to-build-what-it-means-for-the-niles-11-river-states-and-why-its-so-controversial-264665"]," has been one of the most prominent."]},{"k":"p","s":["The massive hydroelectric project was ",["formally initiated","https://theconversation.com/ethiopia-has-struggled-to-build-national-unity-can-its-big-new-dam-deliver-it-265630"]," by Meles Zenawi. He served as president of Ethiopia from 1991 to 1995, and as prime minister from 1995 until his death in 2012. And as early as the 1950s, Emperor Haile Selassie recognised the potential of a dam for Ethiopia’s developmental needs."]},{"k":"p","s":["But can a development project create political unity? Namhla Thando Matshanda ",["notes that","https://theconversation.com/ethiopia-has-struggled-to-build-national-unity-can-its-big-new-dam-deliver-it-265630"]," the dam offers a rare potential rallying point in a country where competing visions of national identity have repeatedly fuelled political tensions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Ethiopia has struggled to build national unity: can its big new dam deliver it?","https://theconversation.com/ethiopia-has-struggled-to-build-national-unity-can-its-big-new-dam-deliver-it-265630"]]}],"chars":4945},"https://theconversation.com/budget-2026-experts-on-what-john-healeys-breathing-space-plan-means-for-households-295377":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"29e3196815e3c35b4d077770cdc8f338b55f41c8d87734c69ff83882793f2e5b","read":"https://theconversation.com/budget-2026-experts-on-what-john-healeys-breathing-space-plan-means-for-households-295377","bytes":196795,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Budget 2026: experts on what John Healey’s ‘breathing space’ plan means for households","by":[{"n":"Alper Kara","r":"Head of Department of Economics, Finance & Accounting, Brunel University of London"},{"n":"Dylan Ryan","r":"Lecturer in Mechanical & Energy Engineering, Edinburgh Napier University"},{"n":"Jonquil Lowe","r":"Visiting Academic, The Open University"},{"n":"Maha Rafi Atal","r":"Adam Smith Senior Lecturer in Political Economy, School of Social and Political Sciences, University of Glasgow"}],"pub":"2026-10-28T17:35:14Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["It was a “breathing space” budget from Chancellor John Healey. In the absence of big surprises or bold change, Healey’s trade-off appears to be small reliefs now in exchange for “fresh hope” in the future. Here’s what our experts made of the chancellor’s first budget."]},{"k":"h","s":["Targeted help with energy costs as bills keep rising"]},{"k":"p","s":["Jonquil Lowe, Visiting Academic, The Open University"]},{"k":"p","s":["This budget took place against a backdrop of global turmoil and rising inflation, driven largely by higher energy costs. These are continuing to squeeze household budgets. From January, the ",["energy price cap","https://www.ofgem.gov.uk/your-energy-supply/your-energy-bill/energy-price-cap-and-standing-charges-explained"]," is predicted ",["to rise by 27%","https://www.uswitch.com/gas-electricity/news/energy-price-cap-january-2027-latest-predictions-and-news/"]," to nearly £2,200 a year for a typical household."]},{"k":"p","s":["Help with energy costs is therefore an important move. This support includes a £100 energy payment for households in England in council tax bands A to D (the devolved governments will receive equivalent funding to replicate this)."]},{"k":"p","s":["There was also a commitment to abolish the standing charge for gas (currently on average ",["30 pence a day","https://www.ofgem.gov.uk/your-energy-supply/your-energy-bill/energy-price-cap-unit-rates-and-standing-charges"],"). The amount will instead be added to the charge for the unit cost of each kilowatt-hour used. This gives households more control over their bills – it will mean that limiting the amount of gas they use will have a bigger effect on reducing their cost. However, one worry is that squeezed households could still risk their health by not heating their homes adequately."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Labour’s manifesto","https://labour.org.uk/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/Labour-Party-manifesto-2024.pdf"]," pledged not to raise taxes on working people. This budget technically kept to that if we assume that working people just receive earnings. But building on last year’s changes, this budget has introduced another increase to the tax rates on interest from savings and rental income. Landlords and some savers ",["will be taxed","https://www.thisismoney.co.uk/money/saving/article-16245973/Savers-landlords-hammered-income-tax-raid-Budget-Healey-ratchets-Reeves-hike-2.html"]," at a basic rate of 24% (currently 20%), higher rate 44% (from 40%) and additional rate 49% (from 45%) from April 2027."]},{"k":"p","s":["This makes it all the more welcome that a proposal last year to cut the cash ISA limit for savers aged under 65 to £12,000 is being abandoned. Everyone, regardless of their age, will still be able to put up to £20,000 a year into a cash ISA (or cash and money funds within a stocks-and-shares ISA) and receive the interest tax-free."]},{"k":"p","s":["The government will also consult on setting up a first-time buyer ISA to replace the Lifetime ISA and help people save for a home. From February 2027, a new scheme called ",["Your First Home","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/your-first-home"]," will provide equity loans for first-time buyers purchasing new properties. The loan, worth 20% of the purchase price, will be tax-free for the first five years. To be eligible buyers must have a household income of no more than £110,000 (£140,000 in London)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["It’s not just rough sleeping – Andy Burnham’s housing plans need to include the ‘hidden homeless’","https://theconversation.com/its-not-just-rough-sleeping-andy-burnhams-housing-plans-need-to-include-the-hidden-homeless-289443"]]},{"k":"p","s":["The budget also delivered a higher tax-free personal allowance for pensioners on the lowest incomes. The new ",["Pension Tax Allowance","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/pension-tax-allowance-explainer"]," will be applied automatically, with HMRC doing the sums. Pensioners with income ",["up to £13,037","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/pension-tax-allowance-explainer/pension-tax-allowance-explainer"]," (the full state pension) will pay no income tax from April 2027. For comparison, for younger people the standard allowance is frozen at £12,570 until April 2031. They would pay £93.40 tax on an income of £13,037."]},{"k":"p","s":["The announcements come on top of a drip feed of “everyday fixes” in the days leading up to the budget. These included ",["reform of carer’s allowance","https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/oct/26/carers-allowance-cliff-edge-abolished-in-the-budget"]," so that carers no longer lose their whole allowance of £86.45 a week once their earnings pass a weekly limit of £204. But it has already emerged that this much-touted change will not come into effect ",["until 2030","https://benefitsandwork.co.uk/news/carers-must-wait-until-at-least-2030-for-fair-treatment"]," while the government updates its IT systems."]},{"k":"h","s":["Small clues that this government is chasing growth"]},{"k":"p","s":["Maha Rafi Atal, Adam Smith Senior Lecturer in Political Economy, University of Glasgow"]},{"k":"p","s":["For years, the UK has faced a structural deadlock: a public that demands robust state services, but which rejects both the broad-based income taxes and pro-growth measures like increased immigration that might fund those services. Under Rachel Reeves’ chancellorship, Labour tried to get around this by raising the necessary taxes indirectly – from everywhere but income. This made it more expensive for businesses to operate, failing to jumpstart growth."]},{"k":"p","s":["In this budget, John Healey has tried a different tack, deploying selective business reliefs alongside a commitment to increased defence spending. Together, these measures make a calculated gamble that state stimulus can rescue the economy from lacklustre growth. In a growing economy, the government gets more tax revenue to fund services even without raising rates, because there’s more economic activity to tax in the first place."]},{"k":"p","s":["The reliefs for business are welcome. Raising the small business rate relief threshold – effectively removing half of all shops, restaurants and gyms from the rates system – provides breathing room for local economies. When paired with the electricity bill reduction ",["for core industries","https://bmmagazine.co.uk/news/business-electricity-bills-industrial-scheme-budget/"]," and the introduction of ",["“founders’ relief”","https://www.gov.uk/government/consultations/founders-relief-technical-consultation"]," for entrepreneurs selling shares in their business, the budget offers some incentives for corporate investment and entrepreneurial risk."]},{"k":"p","s":["The chancellor has also listened in part to businesses that complained of rising costs as a result of the increase in employers’ national insurance and the new measures in the ",["Employment Rights Act","https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2025/36"],". While the ",["minimum wage","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6d93gq1xdgno"]," is set to rise, the government has restored a lower rate for younger workers. This will benefit some businesses in employing people more cheaply, but the government also hopes it will help absorb school-leavers and graduates into the workforce, increasing productivity and reducing the welfare bill."]},{"k":"p","s":["The budget introduces two distinct avenues for the state to proactively stimulate growth. First, through accelerated defence commitments (spending 3% of GDP by 2030, for example), the chancellor is injecting capital directly into domestic supply chains, manufacturing, and high-tech engineering. Second, the roadmap for fiscal devolution offers a regional stimulus by promising to let mayors keep 100% of local business rates by the end of the decade, as well as a share of income tax receipts. This kind of arrangement, to fund infrastructure and attract business, is standard practice in most federalised systems. But its absence has been an unusual quirk of UK devolution."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet, while these measures are constructive, it is not clear that they are enough to reverse the grim reality: growth is stagnant at ",["just over 1%","https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6ae1f7b839d29f3f9b9b3f36/economic-and-fiscal-outlook-october-2026-web-accessible.pdf"]," and the Office for Budget Responsibility predicts it will stay that way."]},{"k":"p","s":["Unlike its predecessor, this government seems to accept that it desperately needs some growth, and therefore some private investment, or public services will fall apart. In this budget, it has signaled some understanding that it may have to meet business halfway to get there. But the fiscal forecast relies on the hope that these stimuli will take effect in time to expand the tax base and preserve public spending before the next election."]},{"k":"p","s":["If they do not, the Treasury has also signaled that like Reeves before him, Healey will resort to spending cuts in the final years of the parliament to balance the books. By deferring that choice, the government has chosen to pray for a growth miracle today, while keeping the threat of real-terms austerity on the horizon tomorrow."]},{"k":"h","s":["Banks to pay more – but Healey bids to keep them lending"]},{"k":"p","s":["Alper Kara, Professor of Banking and Finance, Brunel University of London"]},{"k":"p","s":["One surprise is the relatively modest increase in taxes on banks compared with what financial markets had been expecting. There had been speculation that the government would raise the surcharge on bank profits from 3% to 8%. Instead, the surcharge will increase to 6% for just 15 months, from January 2027. So banks will face a higher tax bill, but a smaller one than many investors had feared."]},{"k":"p","s":["Shares in some ",["major UK banks","https://www.investorschronicle.co.uk/content/d7c3d60f-0aa7-4f7d-a752-0bc2a01ec117?srsltid=AYCX9vKWmMeWLNRNzLxDK-xc6sOFnkaJsolnSBJro8drgweQPPnfdRA8"]," rose as investors welcomed the smaller-than-expected increase. This suggests that investors believe the profitability of banks will be less affected by the tax increase than previously feared."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the decision also reflects the difficult balance facing the chancellor. The government needs more money to support public spending and manage its finances, particularly at a time when ",["borrowing costs remain high","https://www.thetimes.com/business/economics/article/uk-borrowing-costs-highest-2008-qkh6l5xnm"],". Banks are an attractive source of revenue because ",["their profits","https://news.sky.com/story/major-lender-hsbcs-profits-up-32-as-higher-bank-tax-expected-in-budget-13604238"]," have been relatively strong in recent years."]},{"k":"p","s":["And since 2023, ",["higher interest rates","https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/monetary-policy/the-interest-rate-bank-rate"]," have helped many banks earn more. These profits come from the difference between what banks charge borrowers and what they pay savers. So, the government has a reasonable argument that banks should make a greater contribution to public finances. This is especially true when households and businesses have been struggling with high living costs."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, the amount of additional revenue matters. Taxing banks more will generate £1.5 billion in extra income for the Treasury, but it is unlikely to make a substantial difference to the government’s wider spending commitments, such as defence. A temporary increase also means that the additional revenue cannot be relied upon over the longer term."]},{"k":"p","s":["And the next question is who will ultimately pay for this tax increase. Banks could absorb the additional cost through lower profits and reduced returns to shareholders. Alternatively, they might try to protect their profitability by offering lower savings rates, charging higher interest rates on new mortgages and business loans, or increasing fees for customers."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, competition in the banking market will limit how much of the tax banks can pass on to customers. Banks that increase mortgage rates or reduce savings rates risk losing customers to competitors. Given that the surcharge increase will last only 15 months, my view is that banks may prefer to absorb much of the additional cost rather than risk losing market share."]},{"k":"p","s":["The chancellor’s decision to keep the annual cash ISA allowance at £20,000, rather than reducing it to £12,000 as previously planned could also help banks. Cash ISA deposits are an important source of funding for banks and building societies, particularly for mortgage lending."]},{"k":"p","s":["Keeping the higher allowance could help banks retain those deposits and avoid additional funding pressures. This may also be part of the chancellor’s attempt to balance higher bank taxes with the need to keep banks lending to households and businesses."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are also wider considerations. Higher taxes could affect the international competitiveness of the UK banking sector, as banks consider taxation when deciding where to expand their operations. Sustained higher taxation could discourage investment in the UK banking sector, potentially leading to fewer new jobs or even job losses over the longer term."]},{"k":"p","s":["By opting for a smaller and temporary increase, the chancellor appears to have recognised these risks. His decision seems to be aimed at a balance between raising additional revenue and limiting the impact on lending and investment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Relief on energy bills could remove push for heat pumps"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dylan Ryan, Lecturer in Mechanical & Energy Engineering, Edinburgh Napier University"]},{"k":"p","s":["The overall cost of heating with gas ",["will drop for most people","https://bsky.app/profile/alchap.bsky.social/post/3mywgk2e5cc24"],", except for those with larger homes, after the chancellor’s announcement."]},{"k":"p","s":["Once the standing charge, a fixed daily fee, is removed, gas bills will reflect what people actually use. While these lower-than-expected bills will be a welcome relief for bill payers, it could weaken the economic case for households to switch to using heat pumps."]},{"k":"p","s":["There had been rumours of cuts to the ",["boiler upgrade scheme","https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/oct/27/heat-pump-installers-fear-planned-subsidy-cuts-uk-budget"]," intended to help more home owners install heat pumps. However, that didn’t happen. A government report ",["on the scheme","https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/679129c5119e3470fd1e26c7/bus-evaluation-2024-interim-report.pdf"]," said that 65% of property owners who installed heat pumps did so because this grant was available. The report also pointed out that 52% of all recipients of the grant were large detached four-bedroom or bigger homes. So, some sort of reform could be needed."]},{"k":"p","s":["The cut to VAT on ",["electricity","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6x2zrjl7kjno"]," and the £100 paid to those in bands A-D homes will also provide some relief for energy bill-payers."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, energy prices ",["are expected","https://www.uswitch.com/gas-electricity/news/energy-price-cap-january-2027-latest-predictions-and-news/"]," to rise again by the next price cap adjustment in January 2027, due to the Iran war pushing up global energy prices. The government may need to provide some additional relief then. For example, further decoupling electricity prices ",["from the price of gas","https://observer.co.uk/news/national/article/healey-plans-deep-energy-reforms-to-cut-britains-bills"],", as gas often sets the price for electricity."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ultimately, moving energy use away from fossil fuels is a balancing act. But the government is going to have to make further changes if it expects to meet its ",["climate change targets","https://commonslibrary.parliament.uk/research-briefings/cbp-9888/"]," by 2050."]}],"chars":12499},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/singapore":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"6b8368d13f1ca1a469fa27080816454a06dd35a78bff443faabca1a22b57cc44","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/singapore","bytes":67733,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Singapore travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-06T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-03-19T14:08:04+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East"]},{"k":"p","s":["Escalation in the Middle East has caused widespread travel disruption, including airspace closures, delayed and cancelled flights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel plans may be affected, even if your destination is not in the Middle East. Before you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check travel advice for any countries or territories you are transiting through"]},{"k":"li","s":["check for the latest updates from your airline or tour operator"]},{"k":"li","s":["review your travel insurance policy for coverage"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information and sign up for travel advice email alerts"]},{"k":"h","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are severe consequences for drug related crimes in Singapore. Evidence of drug use in your system on arrival or in transit will lead to refusal of entry or arrest. See ",["Entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/singapore/entry-requirements"]," and ",["Safety and security","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/singapore/safety-and-security"]," pages for more information."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/singapore/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Singapore set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Singapore High Commission in the UK","https://www.mfa.gov.sg/london"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Singapore, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are resident in Singapore, there is no minimum passport validity required. ",["Apply for a renewal","https://www.gov.uk/overseas-passports"]," before your passport expires."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Singapore-British dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["Singapore does not recognise dual nationality beyond the age of 21. A citizen of Singapore is required by Singapore law to renounce any other nationalities before the age of 22 in order to retain their Singaporean citizenship."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Singapore without a visa for tourism or business. The ",["Immigration and Checkpoints Authority","https://www.ica.gov.sg/"]," decides who can enter Singapore and how long they can stay. The period of stay permitted is at the discretion of the immigration officer. It is normally between 30 and 90 days for British citizens."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Penalties for overstaying"]},{"k":"p","s":["Penalties for overstaying the time allowed include ",["fines, imprisonment, caning and deportation","https://sso.agc.gov.sg/Act/IA1959?ProvIds=pr15-"]," depending on how long you have overstayed. When arriving and departing Singapore, biometric details, including your fingerprints are recorded electronically."]},{"k":"h","s":["Checks at border control"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must ",["complete an electronic SG Arrival Card","https://eservices.ica.gov.sg/sgarrivalcard/"]," in the 3 days before you arrive in Singapore. This online form asks for travel details and a health declaration. It is illegal to submit a false declaration. Biometric information is also recorded and scanned when you enter and depart Singapore (iris, face and fingerprints)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Screening: Drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Penalties for drug possession, including cannabis, are severe. If you are carrying or transporting drugs, you can be ",["imprisoned, caned or executed","https://sso.agc.gov.sg/Act/MDA1973?ProvIds=Sc2-#Sc2-"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can be screened for drugs in your system on arrival in Singapore, including if you’re in transit. You can be charged with drug consumption or detained without trial even if the drugs were taken in another country, including countries where the use of that particular drug is legal. See ",["Illegal drugs","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/singapore/safety-and-security#illegal-drugs"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ship’s crew"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are different entry requirements if you are ",["crew working on ships, small vessels, or pleasure crafts","https://www.ica.gov.sg/enter-transit-depart/at-our-checkpoints/sea_crew_info"]," arriving at one of Singapore’s ports or marinas."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Singapore, if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"]," for yellow fever, or if you have been in such a country in the previous six days prior to arrival, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination. If you arrive from one of these countries without a certificate, the authorities may put you in mandatory quarantine or refuse you entry to Singapore."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Singapore guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/196/singapore#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Accommodation"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict laws that prevent private homes being used for short-term rental, including for tourists."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Singapore. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal to import ",["controlled drugs","https://sso.agc.gov.sg/Act/MDA1973?ProvIds=Sc1-#Sc1-"],". If convicted, you could be ",["imprisoned, caned or executed","https://sso.agc.gov.sg/Act/MDA1973?ProvIds=Sc2-#Sc2-"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The following items are also illegal to bring into Singapore:"]},{"k":"li","s":["vaporisers and e-cigarettes"]},{"k":"li","s":["tobacco products that are chewed or injected"]},{"k":"li","s":["chewing gum to sell"]},{"k":"li","s":["weapons and ammunition (including empty cartridge cases and air guns)"]},{"k":"li","s":["replica guns, including lighters shaped like a pistol or revolver"]},{"k":"li","s":["radio communications equipment"]},{"k":"p","s":["See the ",["complete list of prohibited items","https://www.customs.gov.sg/businesses/importing-goods/controlled-and-prohibited-goods-for-import"]," on the Singapore Customs website."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Singapore"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Singapore cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Violent crime and theft are rare in Singapore. Take care of your passport. Leave valuables in a hotel safe if possible. Do not leave bags unattended."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["Online scams and phone scams are common and may involve individuals pretending to be officials or bank employees."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Public offences"]},{"k":"p","s":["The public display of the national flags or emblems of other countries is illegal except where a specific exemption has been granted. It is illegal to use the Singapore flag and national symbols in ways considered disrespectful."]},{"k":"p","s":["Police may give you an on-the-spot fine for littering. Acts of vandalism including graffiti carry harsh penalties such as fines, imprisonment and caning."]},{"k":"p","s":["Disrespecting or intimidating a public official can be illegal. There is zero tolerance for bribery in Singapore and any attempt to bribe or otherwise prevent an official from carrying out their duties can lead to arrest."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Use of false ID is illegal in Singapore. Foreigners living in Singapore are issued with an official identity card."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Outrage of modesty"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should avoid any action that could be interpreted as molestation. Penalties for convicted offenders include ",["fines, imprisonment and caning","https://sso.agc.gov.sg/Act/PC1871?ProvIds=pr354-#pr354-."],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some scams involving false claims of molestation and extortion have been reported."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws and bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities do not tolerate drunk and disorderly behaviour. It is illegal to drink alcohol in a public place, besides restaurants, bars and licensed entertainment venues, between 10:30pm and 7am."]},{"k":"p","s":["You could be arrested for:"]},{"k":"li","s":["being found drunk and incapable in public"]},{"k":"li","s":["fighting and becoming a nuisance in public"]},{"k":"li","s":["touching someone inappropriately (whether resulting from drunken behaviour or not)"]},{"k":"li","s":["driving while drunk"]},{"k":"li","s":["drinking in public outside of allowed hours and areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Penalties for convicted offenders include fines, imprisonment and caning."]},{"k":"p","s":["Geylang and Little India are ",["‘Liquor Control Zones’ (PDF)","https://www.police.gov.sg/~/media/spf/files/e-services/boundary_of_little_india_geylang_lca.pdf"],". Drinking in these areas is banned all weekend, on public holidays and on the eve of public holidays."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Vaporisers, smoking and e-cigarette bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["Vapes and e-cigarettes are banned in Singapore. It is illegal to bring them into the country, including for personal use. Those found in possession of vapes or e-cigarettes will have them confiscated and could be fined."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must be 21 or over to ",["purchase, use, own, sell or supply tobacco products in Singapore","https://www.moh.gov.sg/news-highlights/details/minimum-legal-age-for-tobacco-raised-to-21-years-old-from-1-january-2021"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Smoking is banned at all public parks, all beaches and along certain waterways. Orchard Road is a No Smoking Zone. Make sure you smoke in ",["designated areas only","https://www.nea.gov.sg/ORNSZ"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are severe penalties for all drug offences in Singapore, including possession. Carrying even a small amount of drugs can have significant consequences."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can be charged with trafficking (‘intent to sell’) for possessing drugs above a certain amount. You can be detained without trial. Sentences include prison terms, caning and the death penalty, including when transiting through the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Singapore have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items, including cannabis. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"p","s":["See the ",["Misuse of Drugs Act","https://sso.agc.gov.sg/Act/MDA1973?ProvIds=P1III-."]," for information on definitions and penalties."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Arrests and detentions"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re arrested, you might not be allowed to speak with anyone, not even a lawyer while you are questioned."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not offer money to officials. You can face further charges or penalties for any attempt to bribe or prevent an official from carrying out their duties."]},{"k":"p","s":["See our guides on ",["Singapore’s legal and criminal system","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/singapore-prisoner-pack"]," and ",["being arrested or detained abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/arrest-or-detention/arrested-abroad-advice-for-british-nationals"]," to find out how we can help."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re under police investigation, the authorities will take your passport and return it once the investigation is over. If you’re convicted, your passport will be held until you’ve served your sentence."]},{"k":"p","s":["In most cases, you will not be allowed to leave Singapore while the case is open. There is no set timeline for investigations. You must be able to support yourself financially during this period."]},{"k":"p","s":["The British High Commission cannot interfere in the criminal and legal process in Singapore."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Death penalty"]},{"k":"p","s":["A death penalty is a possibility for some offences, including murder and drug trafficking. Penalties for drug offences are severe and possession of even very small quantities can lead to a death penalty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is legal in Singapore. However, the law does not recognise same-sex marriage and partnerships. This means, for example, that foreign residents cannot easily get a dependant’s pass for a same-sex spouse or partner. A child from a same-sex partnership may not be recognised as the child of one or both parents."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is possible to change legal gender in Singapore, subject to medical procedures."]},{"k":"p","s":["LGBT+ support groups and social venues exist in Singapore."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["National Service for British dual nationals and permanent residents"]},{"k":"p","s":["The following are liable for ",["National Service","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/national-service-know-your-obligations"],":"]},{"k":"li","s":["all male Singapore citizens"]},{"k":"li","s":["all male dual nationals aged 20 and under"]},{"k":"li","s":["all male children granted Permanent Resident (PR) status as part of their parents’ PR application"]},{"k":"p","s":["Specific questions on National Service can be put to Singapore’s Central Manpower base, email: contact@ns.sg."]},{"k":"p","s":["For further information, see the ",["Immigration and Checkpoints Authority","https://www.ica.gov.sg/"]," and ",["Ministry of Defence (MINDEF)","https://www.mindef.gov.sg/web/portal/mindef/national-service/discover-ns"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protests and public demonstrations"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid street gatherings and public demonstrations as they will be illegal if they do not have police permission. Foreigners who are not permanent residents are prohibited from attending outdoor demonstrations regardless of police permission. Filming an illegal gathering is forbidden. The wearing of ‘cause-related’ clothing and displaying ‘cause -related’ banners is prohibited in public."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal for foreign nationals to give a talk publicly on ‘racial, communal, religious, cause-related or political topics’ without a permit."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Religions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Both public and private Jehovah’s Witness meetings are illegal in Singapore. It is also illegal to possess any Jehovah’s Witness publication, including a Jehovah’s Witness bible. There are similar measures against the Unification Church and the Shincheonji Church of Jesus."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Singapore, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and read the ",["Singapore Highway Code","https://sso.agc.gov.sg/SL/RTA1961-R11"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can drive with a UK driving licence for up to 30 days. After that you need a ",["1949 international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well as your UK driving licence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as a year of driving experience, minimum age and holding an IDP."]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel. If you’re staying in Singapore on a longer term pass or you’ve become a permanent resident, you must ",["get a Singaporean driving licence","https://www.police.gov.sg/Advisories/Traffic/Traffic-Matters"]," to drive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving under the influence of alcohol carries serious penalties including imprisonment. The traffic police regularly carry out breath tests."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re involved in an accident, you must stay at the scene if there has been damage or injury. You must provide contact details and inform the police within 24 hours."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Arriving or departing by car"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are arriving in a car that is not registered in Singapore, visit the ",["OneMotoring website","https://onemotoring.lta.gov.sg/content/onemotoring/home/driving/entering_and_exiting_singapore/cars-and-motorcycles-registered-in-malaysia.html#extension_staying_more_14days"]," to apply for a vehicle entry permit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Vehicles leaving the country will be checked against police records."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Singaporean authorities will prosecute cases of drunken or antisocial behaviour by air passengers on any aircraft registered in Singapore."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been incidents of ",["piracy and armed robbery","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sea-river-and-piracy-safety"]," against ships in and around the waters of Singapore and the Malacca Strait. Set up secure areas on board and report all incidents to the coastal and flag state authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 995 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Singapore","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/196/singapore#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See what ",["health risks you’ll face in Singapore","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/196/singapore"],", including :"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["chikungunya"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Hand, foot and mouth disease","https://www.healthhub.sg/a-z/diseases-and-conditions/44/hfmd"]," is common in Singapore with more serious outbreaks from time to time. Young children are particularly at risk."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air quality"]},{"k":"p","s":["From June to October Singapore can experience high levels of pollution (haze) from land clearance fires in Indonesia. The haze can cause disruption to local and regional air travel and may have an impact on public health. Monitor the Pollutant Standards Index (PSI) updates and health advisories from the Singapore government."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check to see whether you need approval from the Health Sciences Authority to bring in medication from the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Not all medicines from the UK are available in Singapore. Make sure you have a prescription from your GP and check with a doctor in Singapore who may be able to issue a prescription for a local equivalent. See the ",["HCI Directory","https://eservices.healthhub.sg/healthhubng/public/services/directory"]," for a listing of licensed healthcare institutions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Singapore"]},{"k":"p","s":["Healthcare in Singapore is of a high quality and expensive. English is almost universally spoken in Singapore, so all hospitals, whether private or public, will have English-speaking medical staff."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take enough medication for your stay and carry it in your hand baggage. Make sure you have travel insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment and possible medical repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical providers in Singapore","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/singapore-list-of-medical-facilities-and-practitioners"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Singapore","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-singapore"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you need emotional support during your visit, you can call:"]},{"k":"li","s":["National Care Hotline: 1800 202 6868"]},{"k":"li","s":["Samaritans of Singapore: 1800 221 4444"]},{"k":"li","s":["Mental Health Helpline (Institute of Mental Health): 6389 2222"]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Singapore"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance and fire: 995"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 999"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Singapore"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Singapore"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Singapore"]," in Singapore"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Singapore","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/singapore-bereavement-information"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Singapore","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/singapore-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/singapore/british-high-commission-singapore"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/singapore/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Singapore","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-singapore"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":18841,"change":"Updated information about global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East (‘Warnings and insurance’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/government-to-exempt-all-pensioners-from-cut-to-seniors-health-insurance-rebates-296266":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-25T01:47Z","sha":"c82280bc611bb25fc6979da9b861a60ceb92f83cd37311a762fb52e8b32217e9","read":"https://theconversation.com/government-to-exempt-all-pensioners-from-cut-to-seniors-health-insurance-rebates-296266","bytes":173118,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Government to exempt all pensioners from cut to seniors’ health insurance rebates","by":[{"n":"Michelle Grattan","r":"Professorial Fellow, University of Canberra"}],"pub":"2026-11-25T00:52:50Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["The Greens have won a major concession that will exempt all full and part pensioners from the government’s plan to remove the “top up” to the private health insurance rebate that seniors receive."]},{"k":"p","s":["The deal – one of a series the government is doing to pass legislation through the Senate before the parliament rises for the year on Thursday – will cost $1.5 billion of the original $3 billion in savings."]},{"k":"p","s":["Under the original plan, announced in the budget, people aged 65 and over would receive the same rebate as those younger. The government argued there was no case for puttinig older people on a different footing and said the savings would go into aged care."]},{"k":"p","s":["Health Minister Mark Butler said in a statement on Wednesday:"]},{"k":"p","s":["It was intended that government would invest the $3 billion saved through this measure to deliver more residential aged care beds, more Support at Home Packages, shorter wait times and better care for older Australians. The full investment into aged care announced in the Budget will continue."]},{"k":"p","s":["The government also recognises the realities of the Senate, and reaching agreement was necessary to secure passage of the Bill and deliver these important investments into aged care."]},{"k":"p","s":["We have been clear our intent has been to find responsible savings to invest into Aged Care."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Greens said the deal protected 1.2 million pensioners in a cost-of-living crisis."]},{"k":"p","s":["Greens leader David Shoebridge said about two million insured older Australians lived on less than $37,000 a year. “These cuts would have left people going hungry or missing other essentials with no plan to reinvest in healthcare.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Teal independent Monique Ryan said the decision was a “massive win” for older Australians."]}],"chars":1691},"https://theconversation.com/how-have-the-kangaroos-become-such-an-aflw-powerhouse-and-can-the-demons-upset-them-in-the-grand-final-297636":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-27T05:07Z","sha":"341a40b68027e5a79b03ee83d69db8d68a3774f592bc5e16131397e58ed70648","read":"https://theconversation.com/how-have-the-kangaroos-become-such-an-aflw-powerhouse-and-can-the-demons-upset-them-in-the-grand-final-297636","bytes":181236,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"How have the Kangaroos become such an AFLW powerhouse? And can the Demons upset them in the grand final?","by":[{"n":"Erin Hoare","r":"Associate Professor, The University of Melbourne"}],"pub":"2026-11-27T04:02:57Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Tonight’s ",["AFLW grand final","https://www.afl.com.au/aflw/matches/9081"]," might appear to be an impossible task for Melbourne as the Demons try to upset the league’s powerhouse: two-time reigning premiers North Melbourne."]},{"k":"p","s":["North is the deserved favourite, but the Demons should have some optimism, having secured a grand final berth after a ",["stunning comeback","https://www.afl.com.au/aflw/news/1639040/melbourne-demons-stage-epic-comeback-to-stun-geelong-cats-book-aflw-preliminary-final"]," against Geelong, then beating Carlton in last weekend’s preliminary final."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet Melbourne’s task is enormous: the Kangaroos have lost just once since the 2023 Grand Final (their ",["32-game winning streak","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-09-18/north-melbourne-winning-streak-over-after-shock-loss-to-hawks/107171070"]," was broken by Hawthorn in September). The Roos are striving to become the first team in AFLW history to win three flags in a row."]},{"k":"p","s":["The match at Ikon Park is ",["officially a sell-out","https://www.afl.com.au/aflw/news/1644839/its-a-sellout-no-tickets-left-for-2026-aflw-grand-final-between-north-melbourne-and-melbourne"],", with 13,000 fans ready to cheer on a blockbuster decider."]},{"k":"h","s":["How have North Melbourne become so good?"]},{"k":"p","s":["North Melbourne goes into this match with an unchanged side as it tries to make history. But how have the Kangaroos become so dominant in recent years?"]},{"k":"p","s":["On the field, many regard their midfield as the best in the business, with captain Jasmine Garner and star midfielder Ash Riddell leading the way."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, North Melbourne has become a powerhouse thanks to strong, consistent, supportive club structures for the AFLW program that promote sustained excellence and success. This includes a 2010 partnership with the University of Melbourne, preceding the AFLW competition ",["by six years","https://www.nmfc.com.au/news/237363/aflw-dilena-speech"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["AFLW commentator Chyloe Kurdas recently ",["told the ABC","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-26/aflw-premiership-north-melbourne-in-sight/107427680"]," the Kangaroos’ partnership with Melbourne University – whose players train at North Melbourne’s home base at Arden Street – helped lay the foundation. She said:"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s the groundwork North Melbourne did in 2009, 2010 to invest in the really early days, even before AFLW was on the radar. They used a lot of that intel to build a culture that was ready for women and girls to come into the game at a professional level."]},{"k":"p","s":["This early and genuine commitment to women’s football development, along with its investment in women’s leadership across the club, ",["has been lauded","https://www.espn.com.au/afl/story/_/id/50586639/aflw-grand-final-north-melbourne-roos-dynasty"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although a couple of hours will determine the premiership decider, North Melbourne’s journey to the top has been achieved through longstanding, sociocultural and structural club initiatives."]},{"k":"h","s":["What about the Demons?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Melbourne was one of ",["the pioneers of AFLW","https://www.melbournefc.com.au/news/280242/the-journey-so-far-of-the-aflw"],", and the Demons were pace-setters in the competition’s early days. They regularly played finals and ",["won the 2022 premiership","https://www.melbournefc.com.au/history/honour-board"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For the grand final, veteran Lauren Pearce returns as ruck, having missed the preliminary final due to illness. Icon Tayla Harris will play her 100th match – a remarkable achievement with the shorter AFLW season length. Reaching this milestone takes the best part of a decade, so a grand final for Harris’ 100th match is a fitting occasion."]},{"k":"p","s":["Similar to North Melbourne, the Demons’ sustained success over the competition’s history makes them a well-deserving contender. They have lost just twice in 2026."]},{"k":"h","s":["The psychology of favouritism – and being an underdog"]},{"k":"p","s":["Most agree North Melbourne is the team to beat. Within the locker rooms, it won’t be said out loud, but it will be known."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are many pressures that come with being favourite, including the assumption of winning as default. In other words, the goal can become “don’t lose”. When winning is a baseline expectation, it can bring ",["caution, hesitancy and doubt","https://doi.org/10.1111/spc3.12973"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["How do favourites cope in big matches? The Kangaroos will likely be promoting a focus on usual processes that have got them to this point. They will be sticking to routine and preparing to be genuinely challenged."]},{"k":"p","s":["Their preparation has likely included picturing setbacks before they happen and rehearsing how to respond. Indeed, multi-sensory practices such as imagery, self-talk and attentional practices are ",["believed to enhance performance","https://doi.org/10.1080/1612197X.2023.2168725"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Perhaps surprisingly, Melbourne is likely adopting the same approach. However, its challenge includes building belief and preparing for the occasion, as opposed to handling expectation."]},{"k":"p","s":["For both teams, the message will be centred on self-belief and belonging – that the players are deserving of this opportunity."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dealing with uncertainty is vital"]},{"k":"p","s":["The grand final boasts many elements of a classic showdown. Underdog and heavyweight. Return of a club leader. A possible fairytale celebration for an icon of the sport."]},{"k":"p","s":["That external noise may generate interest, but the players will pay little attention."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Science tells us","https://doi.org/10.1186/s40798-021-00406-7"]," they’re correct to ignore these narratives and focus purely on their preparation, their teammates and their club."]},{"k":"p","s":["Still, optimal preparation is unlikely to decide the outcome of the match. Success in high performance sport is context-specific and largely unpredictable. And what we know about psychology among women athletes is evolving due to ",["historical under-representation","https://bjsm.bmj.com/content/60/18/1409"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Of course, this is an uncomfortable reality for elite athletes who train, prepare, and live in sporting systems that often associate rigidity, routine and preparation as cornerstones of excellence. And in many circumstances they can be."]},{"k":"p","s":["But a grand final brings about a context so unique – high stakes, sell-out crowds, and for many, a career pinnacle – that it is challenging to apply any traditional theory regarding approach to performance."]},{"k":"p","s":["As a psychologist, elite athlete mental health researcher and retired AFLW player, I do propose one view. Among all the unpredictable factors that shape tonight’s grand final, the one that may matter most may be how well players recognise, embrace and accept uncertainty."]},{"k":"p","s":["The team that accepts the unpredictability of the occasion and responds to it without trying to change it will likely emerge victorious."]}],"chars":5554},"https://theconversation.com/coalition-wins-thumping-majority-at-victorian-election-as-labor-and-greens-in-contest-for-opposition-status-297265":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-28T11:11Z","sha":"20756f89ad6063dc82b33924bae7f62ededd4caf9ea2bd080984c24577dc46ef","read":"https://theconversation.com/coalition-wins-thumping-majority-at-victorian-election-as-labor-and-greens-in-contest-for-opposition-status-297265","bytes":178023,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Coalition wins thumping majority at Victorian election as Labor and Greens in contest for opposition status","by":[{"n":"Adrian Beaumont","r":"Election Analyst (Psephologist) at The Conversation; and Honorary Associate, School of Mathematics and Statistics, The University of Melbourne"}],"pub":"2026-11-28T10:37:24Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["With 23% of enrolled voters counted, The ",["Poll Bludger’s results system","https://www.pollbludger.net/vic2026/Results/Projection.htm?"]," is currently projecting that the Coalition will win 62 of the 88 lower house seats at today’s Victorian election, the Greens 11, Labor just 10, One Nation five and there will be one independent. This is based on seats that have either been called for a party or where a party is currently ahead."]},{"k":"p","s":["Current ",["projected final primary votes","https://www.pollbludger.net/vic2026/Results/?"]," are 35.4% Coalition, 19.8% One Nation, 19.0% Labor, 15.1% Greens and 10.7% for all Others. The Greens benefited from Labor’s vote collapse as they do well in inner-city seats, which are the safest seats for left-wing parties."]},{"k":"p","s":["After preferences, the Coalition leads Labor by 58.6–41.4. This currently only reflects two-party swings in seats where Coalition and Labor candidates made the final two. I hope that eventually the electoral commission will provide a Coalition vs Labor two-party count for all seats."]},{"k":"p","s":["At the ",["2022 Victorian election","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Victorian_state_election"],", Labor won 56 of the 88 lower house seats, the Coalition 28 and the Greens four, from a two-party vote of 55.0–45.0 to Labor over the Coalition."]},{"k":"p","s":["Labor has lost current premier Ben Carroll’s Niddrie and former premier Jacinta Allan’s Bendigo East to the Coalition. They are likely to also lose former premier Dan Andrews’ Mulgrave. One Nation leader Warren Pickering has been defeated by the Liberals in Pakenham."]},{"k":"p","s":["The current count reflects votes cast on election day. Pre-poll votes and some postals will be counted later tonight. Vote counting will continue for at least another week."]},{"k":"p","s":["There will be many seats where the electoral commission selected the incorrect two candidates for the final two. These seats will need to be realigned between the correct candidates."]},{"k":"p","s":["Very messy seats, where nobody has much vote share, such as ",["Williamstown","https://www.pollbludger.net/vic2026/Results/LA.htm?s=Williamstown"],", will need to wait until all primary votes are counted and the official distribution of preferences is carried out before a winner can be decided."]},{"k":"p","s":["All 40 upper house seats were up for election in eight five-member regions. Given the lower house results, the Coalition and One Nation combined are very likely to win an upper house majority. I will update this article tomorrow morning with more on the lower and upper houses."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why this result occurred and federal implications"]},{"k":"p","s":["Labor had governed Victoria for the last 12 years and 23 of the last 27, so there was an “it’s time” factor."]},{"k":"p","s":["Former Victorian Labor premier Jacinta Allan was very unpopular. In the ",["Newspoll taken in late July","https://www.theaustralian.com.au/nation/politics/jess-wilson-opens-15point-newspoll-lead-as-victorian-labor-collapses/news-story/b8962613a919752e3d789fd8f1bec001"],", just before Ben Carroll replaced Allan as Labor leader and premier, Allan’s net approval was -46 (71% dissatisfied, 25% satisfied). Her net approval was -42 in the November 2025 Newspoll."]},{"k":"p","s":["While Labor had only trailed by 52–48 in the late July Newspoll, voters at that time hadn’t started to focus on the state election. From mid-October, Labor started to slide in the polls as people focused on the election. Carroll was unable to separate himself from Allan’s legacy."]},{"k":"p","s":["After the May 2025 federal election, I ",["said the two-party swing","https://theconversation.com/labors-win-at-the-2025-federal-election-was-its-biggest-since-1943-with-its-largest-swings-in-the-cities-258402"]," to Labor in Victoria of 1.5% was lower than in any other state except Western Australia. But WA had a 10.6% swing to Labor in 2022, so Victoria’s two-election swing was much lower than in any other state."]},{"k":"p","s":["With the unpopular state Labor government now removed, federal Labor is likely to do better in Victoria at the next election in swing terms relative to the national swing. This election result will help federal Labor."]},{"k":"h","s":["Late Victorian polls"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["Herald Sun reported two late Victorian polls","https://www.heraldsun.com.au/news/victoria/state-election/final-victorian-election-polls-show-coalition-on-track-to-form-majority-government/news-story/b458264b2534bc9c8be90ab8ccf39584"]," on Friday night. A Freshwater poll, conducted November 23–26 from a sample of 1,026, gave the Coalition 34% of the primary vote (up five since the ",["late September Freshwater poll","https://theconversation.com/albaneses-ratings-slump-in-redbridge-poll-after-interest-rate-hike-293202"],"), One Nation 23% (up one), Labor 21% (down three), the Greens 15% (up one) and all Others 7% (down four)."]},{"k":"p","s":["By respondent preferences, the Coalition led Labor by 58–42, a five-point gain for the Coalition."]},{"k":"p","s":["In a three-way preferred premier question, Liberal leader Jess Wilson had 43% (up six), Carroll 27% (down three) and One Nation leader Warren Pickering 17% (up four). In a head to head match-up, Wilson led Carroll by 55–29 (previously 45–33)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The final edition of News Corp’s internal Lighthouse poll, conducted November 9–22 from a sample of “more than 1,200”, gave the Coalition 28% of the primary vote (down three since the ",["November 2–15 Lighthouse poll","https://www.heraldsun.com.au/news/victoria/state-election/final-victorian-election-polls-show-coalition-on-track-to-form-majority-government/news-story/b458264b2534bc9c8be90ab8ccf39584"],"), One Nation 26% (up two), Labor 22% (steady), the Greens 15% (steady) and all Others 9% (up one). No two-party estimate was provided."]}],"chars":4453}};
